WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.920
Episode 2.

00:01.920 --> 00:03.760
In the first episode, we saw how

00:03.760 --> 00:05.799
four Megatron's call for a new

00:05.799 --> 00:08.040
operating system for work.

00:08.040 --> 00:10.160
Today, the first shift from

00:10.160 --> 00:12.519
talented individuals to talented

00:12.519 --> 00:13.560
teams.

00:13.601 --> 00:16.041
Our HR processes are built around

00:16.041 --> 00:18.281
individual talent. Yet work is

00:18.281 --> 00:20.561
done by teams. Talent is no

00:20.561 --> 00:22.280
longer an individual story. It is

00:22.280 --> 00:24.601
a team sport.

00:24.601 --> 00:25.641
And a collection of brilliant

00:25.641 --> 00:27.921
stars does not automatically form

00:27.921 --> 00:30.001
a stable galaxy.

00:30.001 --> 00:31.680
What makes a team perform is the

00:31.680 --> 00:33.840
invisible, the dark matter of

00:33.840 --> 00:36.481
trust and shared values that binds

00:36.481 --> 00:37.801
people together

00:37.801 --> 00:39.561
and keeps the team cohesive,

00:39.561 --> 00:41.361
especially when the storm hits.

00:41.682 --> 00:43.442
This first shift makes teams a

00:43.442 --> 00:45.122
core design principle of our

00:45.122 --> 00:47.442
future operating model. It tackles

00:47.442 --> 00:48.602
several of the underlying

00:48.602 --> 00:50.562
challenges. On the productivity

00:50.562 --> 00:52.921
side, teams must become fluid,

00:52.921 --> 00:54.722
forming and reforming around

00:54.722 --> 00:56.961
missions and fast evolving skills

00:56.961 --> 00:59.122
to deliver organizational agility

00:59.122 --> 01:00.721
at scale.

01:00.721 --> 01:02.401
Knowledge must flow across

01:02.401 --> 01:04.522
generations within teams, not stay

01:04.522 --> 01:06.202
locked in individuals.

01:06.202 --> 01:07.801
And the workplace itself must

01:07.801 --> 01:09.442
become efficient for teamwork

01:09.442 --> 01:10.242
again.

01:10.243 --> 01:12.563
On the human and cultural side,

01:12.563 --> 01:14.162
putting the team first counters

01:14.162 --> 01:16.082
the rise of individualism.

01:16.082 --> 01:17.963
Recognition must be rebuilt around

01:17.963 --> 01:19.762
team results, not just individual

01:19.762 --> 01:20.842
ones.

01:20.842 --> 01:22.802
Finally, people will enjoy coming

01:22.802 --> 01:24.762
to work to join their team, led

01:24.762 --> 01:26.442
by a manager who acts like an

01:26.442 --> 01:27.883
elite sports coach.

01:27.884 --> 01:30.444
To put the team first, we first

01:30.444 --> 01:31.404
need to look at how our

01:31.404 --> 01:33.444
organizations are wired.

01:33.444 --> 01:35.203
For decades, companies have been

01:35.203 --> 01:37.443
built around one operating model,

01:37.443 --> 01:40.364
the traditional top-down hierarchy.

01:40.364 --> 01:41.483
And this is still the model our

01:41.483 --> 01:43.284
HR systems are designed for.

01:43.405 --> 01:45.325
But on the ground, the reality of

01:45.325 --> 01:48.124
teamwork is far more diverse.

01:48.124 --> 01:49.604
Work actually gets done through

01:49.604 --> 01:51.844
matrix organizations, network

01:51.844 --> 01:55.125
structures, and fluid agile teams.

01:55.125 --> 01:56.884
Exactly the fluid teams are

01:56.884 --> 01:59.005
productivity challenges call for.

01:59.205 --> 02:01.165
When our HR systems operate all

02:01.165 --> 02:03.446
these models, these challenges turn

02:03.446 --> 02:05.885
into real gains. We unlock

02:05.885 --> 02:07.525
business agility in a fast

02:07.525 --> 02:09.685
changing environment. We measure

02:09.685 --> 02:11.286
and recognize high performing

02:11.286 --> 02:12.486
teamwork.

02:12.486 --> 02:14.366
And we offer projects and missions

02:14.366 --> 02:15.526
to meet the rapid growth

02:15.526 --> 02:17.926
expectations of new generations.

02:17.926 --> 02:19.926
Missions that also enable lifelong

02:19.926 --> 02:21.926
learning on the job to keep pace

02:21.926 --> 02:23.846
with fast evolving skills.

02:23.967 --> 02:26.207
But the right structures are not

02:26.207 --> 02:29.447
enough. Teams also need moments

02:29.447 --> 02:30.807
that matter.

02:30.807 --> 02:32.807
That is the next shift. See you

02:32.807 --> 02:33.807
in episode three.
